#!/usr/bin/env node
// tt-storm — STORM-W5 storm orchestration entrypoint (suite-only).
//
// The durable storm-specific orchestrator for one shared isolated tamandua
// daemon, one fixture origin/main, Round A (S1-S8 + queued S9/S10) and
// Round B (B1-B5 + phase-gated chaos schedule). This tool OWNS the exact
// campaign, daemon, source/catalog and fixture identities; it records
// intent BEFORE every launch, captures BOTH launch streams for early
// run-id/short-id evidence, re-attaches after its own crash, never
// launches duplicates because a waiter timed out, discovers rugpull
// replacements/children and attributes tokens to roots, and rejects
// ambiguous/missing provenance. All sequencing logic lives in
// tt-storm-engine.mjs (imported here AND by the recording gate with
// injected adapters); this file wires the REAL adapters + operator
// surface.
//
// Modes (explicit):
//   help            side-effect-free usage
//   plan            derive roster/timer numbers from actual registrations +
//                   print the launch plan (read-only)
//   prepare         plan + record the full campaign intent in a fresh dir
//                   under torture-test/var/results (no launches)
//   run             execute a round (A|B) of a prepared campaign; REFUSES
//                   real launches until the campaign is qualified (real
//                   launch requires the coordinator safety approval whose
//                   gate hashes match this checkout — see tt-storm-real.mjs
//                   runOwnedCleanup/approval wiring). There is NO generic
//                   --allow-unqualified reason-string bypass.
//   resume          re-attach a prepared/running campaign by recorded run
//                   id; never relaunches recorded launches.
//   report          forensic bundle into the campaign's results dir
//                   (report.json + report.txt), after owned cleanup
//                   (cleanup failure propagates).
//   arm <phase>     pre-storm arming step (single-flight-prelude |
//                   aged-state | seed-validation) — executes only in the
//                   real rehearsal gate; this run records pending.
//
// Safety posture (STORM-REAL):
//   * EVERY real effect runs inside one admitted immutable PRIVATE exec
//     context (tt-storm-real.mjs buildPrivateExecContext): explicit child
//     env with private HOME/TAMANDUA_STATE_DIR/TAMANDUA_DB_PATH/TMPDIR,
//     absolute binaries, parent TAMANDUA_RUN_ID/worker/step authority
//     stripped, TAMANDUA_TEST_GUARD=1. No operator HOME/state fallback.
//   * run/resume/report/arm perform mode containment (assertModeContained)
//     BEFORE any state write — an escaped/replaced campaign dir or an
//     ownership-changed context is refused.
//   * writes ONLY under this checkout's torture-test/var; refuses path
//     traversal / symlink escapes / destinations outside var; daemon
//     lifecycle belongs to bin/daemon-control; real launch requires the
//     coordinator approval matching the committed safety contract.
//   * DB reads canonicalize run ids at the adapter boundary (public
//     run-<uuid> <-> stored bare uuid) and reject malformed/ambiguous keys.
//   * cleanup is an explicit owned-resource inventory with positive
//     shutdown evidence (runOwnedCleanup); absent/failed/unsettled required
//     cleanup can never mean PASS.

